Keep the stated keys of the window manager file

The writer of the shadow groups dropped a key whose value equalled the default
of the group. The default colour comes from the colour scheme, so a custom
colour that equalled the scheme colour of the moment never reached the file.
The reader hands the type Custom that scheme colour when the file holds no
colour of its own. The shadow therefore followed each later change of the
scheme, while the page still showed Custom.

The page also built an empty set of window manager settings for each save, and
it never read the file into that set. A key that the page owns no row for,
such as Grouping, therefore held its default and lost the line of the user.

Write the Color key for every save of the type Custom. Keep a key that the
file already holds, and drop only a default value that the file never held.
Read the file into the settings before the page copies its rows into them.

Every key keeps its name and its value set, so an older reader still reads the
file.

The change sits on the branch work/wm-kcm of the local tree, as commit 4 of 4.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/kwin/qtcurveshadowconfiguration.cpp b/qt6/kwin/qtcurveshadowconfiguration.cpp
index 02bd1c56..ceaf7c5f 100644
--- a/qt6/kwin/qtcurveshadowconfiguration.cpp
+++ b/qt6/kwin/qtcurveshadowconfiguration.cpp
@@ -115,12 +115,14 @@ void ShadowConfig::load(KConfig *cfg)
     setColorType((ColorType)m_colorType);
 }
 
-#define WRITE_ENTRY(name, field) do {           \
-        if (def.field == field) {               \
-            group.deleteEntry(name);            \
-        } else {                                \
-            group.writeEntry(name, field);      \
-        }                                       \
+// Keep a key that the file already holds, because the user saw its value.
+// Drop a key that the file never held and that carries the default value.
+#define WRITE_ENTRY(name, field) do {                   \
+        if (group.hasKey(name) || def.field != field) { \
+            group.writeEntry(name, field);              \
+        } else {                                        \
+            group.deleteEntry(name);                    \
+        }                                               \
     } while (0)
 
 void ShadowConfig::save(KConfig *cfg)
@@ -137,7 +139,9 @@ void ShadowConfig::save(KConfig *cfg)
     if (m_colorType != CT_CUSTOM) {
         group.deleteEntry("Color");
     } else {
-        WRITE_ENTRY("Color", m_color);
+        // The default colour comes from the colour scheme of the moment, so
+        // the file must hold the custom colour even when the two agree.
+        group.writeEntry("Color", m_color);
     }
 }
 
diff --git a/qt6/kwinconfig/qtcurvekwinconfig.cpp b/qt6/kwinconfig/qtcurvekwinconfig.cpp
index c199579b..caf904ec 100644
--- a/qt6/kwinconfig/qtcurvekwinconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt6/kwinconfig/qtcurvekwinconfig.cpp
@@ -191,6 +191,9 @@ void KWinConfig::save(KConfig *c)
 
     KWin::QtCurveConfig config;
 
+    // The page does not own every key of the group. Read the file first, so
+    // that a key which the page does not show keeps the value of the file.
+    config.load(cfg, c ? KWIN_GROUP : nullptr);
     config.setBorderSize((KWin::QtCurveConfig::Size)borderSize->currentIndex());
     config.setRoundBottom(roundBottom->isChecked());
     config.setOuterBorder((KWin::QtCurveConfig::Shade)outerBorder->currentIndex());
